# Reverse proxy for the "Cloudflare DNS proxy (orange cloud) in front of a
# VPS" deployment — see docker-compose.prod.yml and the README's Deploying
# section. Replace the placeholder domain with your real one.
#
# `tls internal` makes Caddy mint its own self-signed cert rather than
# requesting one from Let's Encrypt. That's deliberate: Cloudflare's edge is
# the only thing that ever talks to this cert (real visitors only ever see
# Cloudflare's own certificate), and Cloudflare's "Full" SSL/TLS mode
# encrypts that hop without validating the origin cert's chain — so a
# self-signed cert here is enough to stop the Cloudflare-to-VPS hop from
# being plain HTTP, with none of the DNS-01/HTTP-01 ACME complications that
# come from Cloudflare's proxy sitting in front of a Let's Encrypt challenge.
# Trade-off: this is "Full", not "Full (strict)" — good enough for a
# solo-operator deploy; if you want strict chain validation instead, swap
# this for a Cloudflare Origin CA certificate (dashboard: SSL/TLS -> Origin
# Server) and point `tls` at the two file paths instead of `internal`.
store.okhubtech.com {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy video-store:4100
}
